      "math_academy_id": "q-110598",
      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14205615/assets/b0189edb7d5582896a6b56623fa5b33c1dc9b65ff3d8ccaf634df452a72d9e0f.png)\n\nThe figure above shows part of the graph of $y=f(x)$ which is defined on the interval $x\\in [-3,3].$ Given that $f(x)$ is even, which of the following gives the complete graph of $y=f(x)?$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that the graph of an even function must be symmetric about the $y$-axis.\n\nSo, we can obtain the missing part of the graph by reflecting the given part over the $y$-axis. \n\nTherefore, the complete graph of the function is shown below.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14205615/assets/22914a2693ec654474ca8572587386de4c35ae3feb6663bd1c915c29bbf9e5dd.png)",
